{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves","id":1465837,"title":"Overly Sarcastic Productions - Premodern Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-29T15:00:52-07:00","id":1465837,"title":"Overly Sarcastic Productions - Premodern Werewolves","content":"This dropped today:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4mm0KyaovhY&amp;ab_channel=OverlySarcasticProd uctions\" data-code=\"4mm0KyaovhY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4mm0KyaovhY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This is a fun video, and jives a lot with my recent research around how magic is actually seen outside the fantasy genre: mostly as unsanctioned religious ritual that really has nothing to with rewriting the fundamentals of reality.<br /> <br /> So, open thread for people to discuss this. What kinds of weird overlaps have you done with Uratha and folk-religious practice? Have you ever brought Dracula into a campaign... as a Werewolf? Would you consider using the Hisil as a kind of rare gateway into the Astral so that you could fight witches in the battlefield of dreams?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T18:12:05-07:00","id":1465857,"title":"","content":"Well, the fantasy genre is all about made up mythologies and divorced of religion, not to mention how it takes into a pseudo-scientific undertones in RPGs in particular.<br /> <br /> Not quite what you asked for, but years ago when STing a Requiem chronicle in Rio de Janeiro instead of using Uratha or Garou i made the <i>An'yang\u00e1</i>, my own brand of shapeshifter mixing bits &amp; pieces of native american folklore in the form of shachangers divided by families of transforming animal, all dedicated to hunting the walking dead, &quot;to bring them back&quot; to the <i><b>Jurema </b></i>sacred trees that serve as bridges between the worlds of living and dead, re-empowering the trees by putting them to sleep between their roots, returning the crimson sap of stolen lives in their veins back to its rightful place in the world below - and the an'yang\u00e1, that renewed their magic periodically with potions made from the Jurem\u00e1's leafs and sap.<br /> <br /> Mechanically all the &quot;clans&quot; &amp; &quot;tribes&quot; were treated as a single Ghoul family with Protean in its discipline set, but segregated across family or &quot;patron animal&quot; lines depending on locality and their particular history of conflict between themselves and the walking dead in a region, what could lead to cycles of destruction, reconstruction &amp; rebirth of varied results. the conconctions made from the Jurema (that is a series of local species with all kinds of interesting lore in folk religion and medicine) a form of <i>Lacrima</i>. (a kind of vitae facsimile originated from the sap of <i>Mandragora</i>, aka, Ghoul Plants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-29-2021, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T22:00:52-07:00","id":1465868,"title":"","content":"Mmm, my country has a suspicious lack of wolves in folklore, despite them clearly having existed and caused much mayhem. Probably has to do with how tigers, foxes, and bears dominate folklore here.<br /> <br /> Closest thing I can think of are tying them to Mongolian culture, the Yacha (ie. Yaksa) in Buddhism, and a story where two great \u2018fire dogs\u2019 each takes bites out of the sun and the moon despite being burned and frostbite-d respectively, though the latter is obviously non-Forsaken material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T10:47:09-07:00","id":1465923,"title":"","content":"I love the OSP channel. There are some errors in the part about the Inquisition, but hey, Red's not the History Girl of the channel and it wasn't the focus of the video.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465857#post1465857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">STing a Requiem chronicle in Rio de Janeiro instead of using Uratha or Garou i made the <i>An'yang\u00e1</i>, my own brand of shapeshifter mixing bits &amp; pieces of native american folklore in the form of shachangers divided by families of transforming animal, all dedicated to hunting the walking dead, &quot;to bring them back&quot; to the <i><b>Jurema </b></i>sacred trees that serve as bridges between the worlds of living and dead, re-empowering the trees by putting them to sleep between their roots, returning the crimson sap of stolen lives in their veins back to its rightful place in the world below - and the an'yang\u00e1, that renewed their magic periodically with potions made from the Jurem\u00e1's leafs and sap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked it, just let me point some things out.<br /> <br /> 1- <i>An'yang\u00e1</i> isn't a spelling any Brazilian would manage naturally. The correct spelling is <i>Anhang\u00e1</i>, and it affects the pronunciation, as you won't actually make the nasal sound right at the first A, but during the not-quite-a-Y-but-close-enough-I-guess sound.<br /> <br /> 2- <i>Jurema</i> isn't quite a thing in Rio. Both the plants called Jurema and the syncretic religious practices associated with them are from the North-East region of the country, with very little influence south of the state of Bahia. You have already quite a number of big cities there where this would fit better (including my wife's birthplace, Recife, in the state of Pernambuco).<br /> <br /> 3- The <i>Jurema</i> plants are actually a number of species not always related. Of importance, the teas and infusions used in <i>Jurema</i> rituals are from shrubs from the <i>genus mimosa</i>, while the trees are <i>genus acacia</i>. At neither of those <i>genii</i> they're common plants, the <i>genii</i> are actually named after the most common names for plants on them, so <i>Jurema</i> can be considered a false <i>genus.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T12:48:46-07:00","id":1465936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465923#post1465923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- <i>An'yang\u00e1</i> isn't a spelling any Brazilian would manage naturally. The correct spelling is <i>Anhang\u00e1</i>, and it affects the pronunciation, as you won't actually make the nasal sound right at the first A, but during the not-quite-a-Y-but-close-enough-I-guess sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Won't deny i threw a &quot;sort of pseudo-archaic spelling &amp; pronunciation but not really&quot; here for partial obfuscation of the reference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465923#post1465923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- <i>Jurema</i> isn't quite a thing in Rio. Both the plants called Jurema and the syncretic religious practices associated with them are from the North-East region of the country, with very little influence south of the state of Bahia. You have already quite a number of big cities there where this would fit better (including my wife's birthplace, Recife, in the state of Pernambuco).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, took some liberty here, the state capitals and major cities of the Northeast would indeed be more regionally appropriate to tie up with the Jurema-related traditions. But the game was already set in Rio de Janeiro, so i threw a &quot;much of what is now specific to the northeast was present through much of the Mata Atlantica - and most of the coast - during the colonial period and before&quot; conceit and ran with it for convenience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465923#post1465923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- The <i>Jurema</i> plants are actually a number of species not always related. Of importance, the teas and infusions used in <i>Jurema</i> rituals are from shrubs from the <i>genus mimosa</i>, while the trees are <i>genus acacia</i>. At neither of those <i>genii</i> they're common plants, the <i>genii</i> are actually named after the most common names for plants on them, so <i>Jurema</i> can be considered a false <i>genus.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, also very true. I very much exploited that with the specific sort of Jurema used by each cell/clan/family unit of Anhang\u00e1 would vary and could be a point of contention or nexus of identity between different groups. Also, vitae-infused plants can develop in ways unlike their relatives found in nature, depending on time and variety of kindred staked in their roots.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cultists and most supernatural creatures are not much, if any, for academic or taxonomic rigueur&quot; is the way i roll 9 times out of 10, with Espiritist-anarchist Dragolescu in S\u00e3o Gon\u00e7alo, a isle where the group suicide of a UFO cult (inspired by Cultura Racional - the <i>Universo em Desencanto</i> people) would bring across something that claims to be their otherwordly guides and a group of werewolves that worship <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Christopher\" target=\"_blank\">Saint Cristov\u00e3o</a> being some other weird fun bits from CotD (nWoD back then) books with tweaked for fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-30-2021, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T15:55:08-07:00","id":1465945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465868#post1465868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closest thing I can think of are tying them to Mongolian culture, the Yacha (ie. Yaksa) in Buddhism, and a story where two great \u2018fire dogs\u2019 each takes bites out of the sun and the moon despite being burned and frostbite-d respectively, though the latter is obviously non-Forsaken material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, lodges have considerable room for myths that veer in directions deviating from the typical Forsaken mythos as we know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T16:13:12-07:00","id":1465947,"title":"","content":"In Argentina they got little interesting thing to add to the legend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2014/12/29/373834462/argentine-president-takes-on-godson-to-keep-werewolf-legend-at-bay\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2014/12/29/kirchner1_wide-9286486473f991ceecf954becaeab14ae51fc110-s1400-c100.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2014/12/29/373834462/argentine-president-takes-on-godson-to-keep-werewolf-legend-at-bay\" target=\"_blank\"> Argentine President Takes On Godson &mdash; But Not To Keep Werewolf At Bay </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2014/12/29/373834462/argentine-president-takes-on-godson-to-keep-werewolf-legend-at-bay\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2014/12/29/373834462/argentine-president-takes-on-godson-to-keep-werewolf-legend-at-bay </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The tradition, it now appears, is from czarist Russia and began during mass Russian migration to Argentina in the early 20th century. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:21:35-07:00","id":1465950,"title":"","content":"I think in terms of reconciling Forsaken with presentations of real life folk beliefs about werewolves, that's a place where Wolf-Blooded would end up being prominent, particularly how Second Edition focused on them as basically the game's place to store most of those motifs.<br /> <br /> If I was thinking about a historical basis for it, it would be in an idea that for the longest time the distribution of Uratha and Wolf-Blooded was such that you got far more of the latter running around without enough of the former to gather them up into packs. That in a drastically less urbanised world, Uratha had a tendency to sequester themselves, but overall human population densities meant that Wolf-Blooded appeared frequently in more dense groups, and tended to stick with them. Heterodox religious practice would be a tendency to try and reconcile what was familiar to them with any new (but probably fairly limited) insights into the Shadow and spirits as a whole.<br /> <br /> That and I'd say it's the kind of thing people often mistake Uratha Rites for, considering how Second Edition has diversified their forms. Heck, given the range of options for learning them and the very nature of their origin, it could well be that Uratha at times ended up learning Rites out of the practices of religious groups, and an association between the two arising from things like the Uratha element distorted by seeing from afar, hearing about it second hand, or being filtered through Lunacy, as well as any more visible Wolf-Blooded present at the margins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:42:14-07:00","id":1465955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465945#post1465945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly, lodges have considerable room for myths that veer in directions deviating from the typical Forsaken mythos as we know it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would hunting Lunes and Helions (&quot;taking bites out of the Sun and the Moon&quot;) count, thought? Though now that you mention it, with how Urdaga approach their prey in 2E, maybe it does...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465950#post1465950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in terms of reconciling Forsaken with presentations of real life folk beliefs about werewolves, that's a place where Wolf-Blooded would end up being prominent, particularly how Second Edition focused on them as basically the game's place to store most of those motifs.<br /> <br /> If I was thinking about a historical basis for it, it would be in an idea that for the longest time the distribution of Uratha and Wolf-Blooded was such that you got far more of the latter running around without enough of the former to gather them up into packs. That in a drastically less urbanised world, Uratha had a tendency to sequester themselves, but overall human population densities meant that Wolf-Blooded appeared frequently in more dense groups, and tended to stick with them. Heterodox religious practice would be a tendency to try and reconcile what was familiar to them with any new (but probably fairly limited) insights into the Shadow and spirits as a whole.<br /> <br /> That and I'd say it's the kind of thing people often mistake Uratha Rites for, considering how Second Edition has diversified their forms. Heck, given the range of options for learning them and the very nature of their origin, it could well be that Uratha at times ended up learning Rites out of the practices of religious groups, and an association between the two arising from things like the Uratha element distorted by seeing from afar, hearing about it second hand, or being filtered through Lunacy, as well as any more visible Wolf-Blooded present at the margins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm sold. In my brainspace, the Fox-Eyed are 'mistaken' Wolf-Blooded who developed a tradition of being descended from ancient pre-Confucian vulpine monster-gods. Pray that you won't be the next target of their chimerical satires...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:50:27-07:00","id":1465959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465837-overly-sarcastic-productions-premodern-werewolves?p=1465947#post1465947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Argentina they got little interesting thing to add to the legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>The seventh son curse is an old staple from Iberian cultures, and became about werewolves during America's colonization. We have that here in Brazil, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}